# ztOS on the Galaxy M20 (m20lte): the kernel is ztOS's own boot image, not a
# package (see devices/m20lte/scripts/build-boot.sh).
# for looking at the M20's I2C devices (backlight, gauge, touch) during bring-up
i2c-tools
# GNOME's adaptive (libadwaita) apps: they fit a phone's width. Music and
# podcast players wait for sound; KDE's mobile apps would add a second
# toolkit (Qt and its web engine). They draw in software for now
# (GSK_RENDERER=cairo in os/overlay-m20lte/etc/ztos/session.env).
gnome-calculator
gnome-clocks
gnome-weather
gnome-calendar
gnome-maps
gnome-text-editor
loupe
foliate
celluloid
newsflash
# Bluetooth (devices/m20lte/drivers/scsc-bt makes the hci_dev)
bluez
bluez-utils
# A browser made for phones (GNOME Web: adaptive, address bar at the bottom)
epiphany
